  Add utility function to save/load all models/optimizers stored in an accelerator
Hi all,
I'm not from the nlp regime, but I love the concept of accelerate. However, I would like to propose some new features.

Since every accelerator.prepare call will essentially store a reference of the object in accelerator. It should be easy to implement a save_all()/load_all() utility that saves/loads all the pytorch module and optimizer state dicts to/from a checkpoint. This utility also has the benifit to save and load the state dict of grad scaler, and potentially any other internal states (which are all agnostic to accelerator users)

I guess the singature could look something like `def save_all(self, filename: str, dict_of_additional_usr_data: Dict[str, Any])`

What do the maintainers think of this utility?
